{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1523695-classes-of-magic-subsystem","id":1523695,"title":"Classes of Magic [Subsystem]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-06T05:25:57-07:00","id":1523695,"title":"Classes of Magic [Subsystem]","content":"So for quite a while now I have been thinking about how to adapt certain D&amp;D class ideas that I had in mind into a system. Obviously, I considered D&amp;D as a system, but I had too many variations that I wanted to examine and making 20 levels of a class sounded like a headache to me (and I also have some sour taste in my mouth from D&amp;D lately so also that). As such, I invested a lot of time to conceptually trying to work around it, almost considering to make my own system (or use a very flexible one as a base, such as Savage Worlds), when it occurred to me that I do know of a system that allows a flexible use of magic and which probably could be modified to give the aesthetics that I want without dealing too much with the system. So yeah, I decided to modify M:tAw by adding a Kith-like splat to Mage based around D&amp;D classes- Calls.<br /> <br /> Basically, Calls are certain wrappings you add on the Mage template during character creation, which encourages magic to be used in certain manners by enforcing a set of Conditions which are gained by increasing Gnosis (currently up to 5, because let's avoid &quot;epic&quot; levels for now), meant to &quot;replicate&quot; the &quot;level benefits&quot; in D&amp;D Classes. The Gnosis Conditions include an additional way to gain Mana, a Condition which increase Paradox chances ion certain occasions, and two more Conditions to influence how the Awakened casts magic. All the Conditions which don't grant Mana grant Arcane Beats instead, like Paradox Conditions. Additionally, Calls have a special Act of Hubris for the Medium Wisdom range (meant, again, to shape behaviour), and their own Magical Symbolism, including 3 additional Rote Skills and Call Tools. In case the Call rote Skills overlap with their Order Rote Skills, the character gains a Specialty in that skill for free.<br /> <br /> While the Calls are meant to coexist alongside Paths and Orders and not to replace them, they do east a bit of territory from both sides, especially parts of the Paths as they take certain nicknames (such as Witch, Warlock of Thaumaturge) and use them for something else. As it is a fan project with a certain goal I don't mind it, but in case it is a problem I suggest just taking it into account that when you had another significant splat into the system, it is going to step on some toes. Obviously, suggesting on refining those Calls will be welcome.<br /> <br /> Anyway, while Calls are meant to represent some modifications to the template and different views for what is &quot;magic&quot; in the context of the game, there are still some &quot;ground rules&quot; which Calls need to obey, imo, to keep the themes and integrity of the game. This is what I called the &quot;Postulates of Magic&quot;, which are presented below together with the first Call that I wrote- the Rogue (there are currently around 38 different Calls, but I hope that some will fall out as I will discover that they have too much of overlap and can't stand on their own). Hope you'll like it!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>The Postulates</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Magic Exists</b></span><br /> <br /> The existence of magic is a fundamental fact of the universe. While many cultures, orders and cults have tried to define it through numerous ways or even deny it, the underlying fact is that magic is an active force and an elemental part of reality, serving as the \u201cpower of creation\u201d.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">As Above, So Below</span></b><br /> <br /> Magic can not be understood, defined or formulated, yet it can only be activated through understanding, definition and formulation. Different sects have different approaches, and those approaches are the ones which allow magic to be actualized- a Fallen understanding serving as a channel to a Supernal truth. As such, the unexplained is being explained, even though falsely, and that false understanding is what guides towards Ascension.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>All Lies are Equal</b></span><br /> <br /> As magic transcends understanding, all approaches to magic are equally false. None is \u201ccloser\u201d to truth as all provide different paths to truth. None of them sins towards magic as magic has no preference and no morals. By claiming to be more superior than the others, they actively undermine their own truth, becoming false in the process- yet one must commit to a certain Lie and claim it to be true, or magic will not be able to be actualized.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>The Ancients Failed</b></span><br /> <br /> Once, magic was free. Now, the world is Fallen. The ancients which once guided the world through magic have failed their faithful, either destroying the old world or rising to become tyrannical gods. This, however, never happened- there was never a utopian world of magic which had fallen from grace, there was never a paradise from which humans were banished. Yet it is a living fact within magic that there were ancients, and that they are now gone, forever lost. Each society defines the \u201clost utopia\u201d according to their own terms, be it Atlantis, Eden, Lemuria or whatever fits their own interpretation of magic.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Hubris Demands Compensation</b></span><br /> <br /> Acts of hubris sin against the very nature of reality and the foundation of magic. No methodology can escape this demand, for this is the punishment which fell upon the ancients, forming a law upon the heavens. Any careless use of magic would end up with twisting, if not shattering, the very nature of reality, allowing it to be corrupted and become less true and more false. This act is what is sometimes called a \u201cParadox\u201d - a true state forced upon a false reality and vice versa - yet different groups have their own terms to explain the failure of magic when it is used without the proper wisdom.<br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Rogue</b></span><br /> <br /> <i><b>Magic is Serendipitous</b></i><br /> <br /> Magic is not learned- it occurs, drawn to the Awakened who are favoured by the Powers that Be. The Awakening is not a part of calculated mechanisation of the gods, it is a stochastic process, where the people in the right place and the right time are simply lucky enough to stumble into a Mystery Play, and are lucky enough to survive it as well. Some people win the lottery, others win the genetic lottery- it makes sense that some souls win the Supernal lottery as well. And those who are lucky enough to Awaken just keep luck drawn towards them. It is just like evolution- the lucky survive, and the more they survive the lickeir they will be.<br /> <br /> <br /> Rogues generally don\u2019t view magic as an analytical or mystical process- magic just happens, and it generally serves in favour of the rogue unless there are other powers in play. As such, the magic of the rogues is rarely a vulgar one- it almost always emerges as part of reality, disrupting the fabric of the Fallen as little as possible. Oh, sure, rogues often have their small ceremonies and superstitions- knock on wood, spit when a black cat passes, wear your lucky shirt and so forth, but those are just methods to draw luck. When they negotiate, they just know the right words that will allow them to open the road to their target;s heart. When they are getting shot, the bullets accidently ricochet and start a fireball that consumes their enemies. When the dead claw their way from the grave with desire for vengeance, the rogue just happens to throw salt upon them, and somehow it is enough to banish them back to the hungry Underworld. Magic is an instinct, an hunch, and should be understood the same way.<br /> <br /> <br /> While being lucky is obviously beneficial, it is hubris to think there is no cost for one\u2019s fortune. Rogues who often abuse their luck start to draw the ire of the gods, as they put themselves into troubles out of faith they will be saved. While sometimes they just die as their luck fails them, much worse events take place- luck is invoked in their favour when by all chance, it should be impossible for them to succeed. Their demand for fortune overrides reality itself, and by doing so, reality twists and breaks and the gods rage, demanding compensation. That\u2019s when the Abyss bursts into the world- balancing the luck of the rogue with much needed misfortune.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Gnosis Conditions</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Bountiful Luck</b></span><br /> <br /> Rogues dance on the strings of fate, allowing them to find enlightenment at pure chance. Once per chapter, when making a role related to their Call Rote Skills and achieving an Exceptional Success, they can choose to \u201cliquify\u201d their luck into Mana, gaining an amount of Mana equal to their number of successes in the roll instead of the regular effect of an Exceptional Success. The role will still be treated as a Success in whatever it was meant to achieve.<br /> <b>Source</b>: Adopting the Rogue Call<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Out of Pattern</b></span><br /> <br /> Rogues view magic as happy coincidences bestowed upon them through randomness and chance, and trying to enforce that act through force disrupts their delicate symbolism. When casting magic in a way which visually violates the natural laws, add 2 dice to their Paradox roll.<br /> <b>Source</b>: adopting the Rogue Call<br /> <b>Arcane Beat</b>: the character avoids solving a problem using magic at a significant cost in order to avoid using it vulgarly.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Sly Hands</b></span><br /> <br /> Rogues put their lives in the hands of chance, betting on lives on a daily basis. When failing in a roll which involves a Speciality, the Rogue may choose to take a Dramatic Failure instead of a regular Failure as normal- yet by doing so, they may choose to gain an Arcane Beat instead of a regular Beast.<br /> <b>Source</b>: reaching Gnosis 3 as a Rogue<br /> <b>Arcane Beat</b>: as described<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Chained by Events</b></span><br /> <br /> Rogues are so used to relying on their luck that they become imprints of it- they must follow a set of rules, or otherwise they\u2019ll fall from the Pattern and become forsaken by the luck that carries them. Choose a certain obligation, equivalent for the Ban of a Rank 3 ephemeral entity. If the rogue is to violate their Ban, their Gnosis is considered to be 2 dots lower for all purposes besides Mana capacity (but does affect Mana per turn) until the end of the Scene.<br /> <b>Source</b>: reaching Gnosis 5 as a Rogue<br /> <b>Arcane Beat</b>: following the Ban at the cost of causing significant damage to your goals or allies.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Act of Hubris</b></span><br /> <br /> <i><b>Wisdom 4-7, Medium / Understanding</b></i><br /> <br /> Rogues are tied to the natural flow of the universe, and that understanding could lead them to gain further intuition about what might happen. Disrupting an event which should naturally happen as understood through prophecy, dedicated knowledge or common sense, is considered an Act of Hubris on their part. Whether it is stopping a cat from devouring a pigeon, convincing a person to turn away from their true love or turning a poor person to rich one, when performed through the acts of magic (or when it is known to be destined through the acts of magic), those acts are nothing more than a hubris.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Magic Symbolism: Taking a Chance</b></span><br /> <br /> Rogues always lurk between the cracks in reality, being favoured by fortune as they put themselves in peril. As such, rogues are always driven to situations where it is all or nothing, gambling on their lives to either win it all or fall to the Abyss. However, that doesn\u2019t mean that they are fools- they always make sure that luck is in their favour, drawing it through their personal rituals and charms, as well as maintaining that they are skillful enough at getting out of trouble as they are in getting into them, just to make sure they have a way out if and when luck will fail them.<br /> <br /> Call Tools: Superstitions, lucky charms, dice and games<br /> <br /> Call Rote Skills: Enigmas, Larceny, Socialise<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Philosophy of Magic</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>On the Paths</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Acanthus</b>: it is good to truly understand what \u201cluck\u201d means, but you should be careful to not try and control it as much.<br /> <br /> <b>Mastigos</b>: making a friend from a foe is the greatest skill you\u2019ll have in your arsenal- just charm them with a wink and a smile and they are yours.<br /> <br /> <b>Moros</b>: it is always good to have a card in your sleeve- such as an \u201cinfinite gold\u201d cheat code or having a friendly ghost whispering in your ear.<br /> <br /> <b>Obrimos</b>: we are favoured by magic itself. The gods have blessed us, and they are on our side when all hell breaks loose.<br /> <br /> <b>Thyrsus</b>: surviving a fatal wound or gaining the favour of an ancient good are all privileges granted to us, and which we shouldn\u2019t abuse.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>One the Orders</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Adamantine Arrow</b>: war is nothing but a game, and there is no better test for your luck than surviving a battle.<br /> <br /> <b>Guardians of the Veil</b>: providence must be cherished- use it carelessly, and it may run out, and then the Abyss will come to catch you and no one will hear you scream.<br /> <br /> <b>Mysterium</b>: knowledge is power- you shouldn\u2019t take a bet before making sure you stack the deck in your favour.<br /> <br /> <b>Silver Ladder</b>: luck has blessed us with many gifts, which we should use at the benefit of those less fortunate than us.<br /> <br /> <b>Free Council</b>: everyone has their own methods to draw luck and ward against misfortune. We should learn from them, instead of focusing on ourselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Seers of the Throne</b>: luck is a gift of the Exarch, meant for their servants- and as they grant it to those worthy, they can easily also take it away.<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere</b>: luck should be at the hands of the worthy- and as such, it should be taken from those misusing it.<br /> <br /> <b>Scelesti</b>: the Abyss is not the misfortune incarnated- it is true providence, and infinity of possibilities. Drink deep from it and prosper.<br /> <br /> <b>Banishers</b>: luck grants us so much, yet some dare to demand more than they deserve, and burn the world in the process. This hubris must be punished.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>On the Arcana</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Death</b>: death always accepts gambles.<br /> <br /> <b>Fate</b>: always in the right place and the right time.<br /> <br /> <b>Forces</b>: all that you need to start an inferno is a spark.<br /> <br /> <b>Life</b>: the human body can achieve great wonders when wired correctly.<br /> <br /> <b>Matter</b>: with the right set of tools everything can be shaped.<br /> <br /> <b>Mind</b>: say the right words and you can easily open the door to your enemy\u2019s heart.<br /> <br /> <b>Prime</b>: solve the equations, make sure to not divide by zero, and follow the maths.<br /> <br /> <b>Space</b>: just follow your intuition and the world will bend for your will.<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit</b>: even a lesser god can\u2019t withstand flattery<br /> <br /> <b>Time</b>: what is prophecy if not remembering but backwards?<br /> <br /> <b>Abyss</b>: the gap between the lucky and the unlucky<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T06:00:10-07:00","id":1523696,"title":"","content":"Interesting project! Though I would've framed Rogues with Mastigos-ness rather than Acanthus-ness.<br /> <br /> I also feel the mini-template as is relies a bit too much on Conditions, though I can't think of succinct replacements... Perhaps giving a few free Praxes, and one or two mandatory Inurements, could replace some of the Gnostic Conditions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T07:49:32-07:00","id":1523710,"title":"","content":"Before making a new Condition, you should always ask yourself:<br /> <br /> How does the gameplay experience benefit from this being a named Condition with a resolution or beat trigger, instead of just being a general mechanic, keeping in mind that the Condition system best functions when a minimal number of simple and flexible Conditions are in play at a given time, each immediately relevant to what is going on in the story, and each impelling player and character behavior towards interesting and genre-appropriate narrative events and plot beats?<br /> <br /> (You may ask: &quot;Don't most of the Conditions in the books fail this test?&quot;<br /> Yes, they do.)<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what use the Postulates are, as they seesaw between simply restating the Awakening setting premise and replacing parts of it with an overbroad shrug. They seem self-contradictory (if all lies are equal, how are there living facts within magic defining the lost Time Before? if no teaching is a sin for magic knows not sin, why is there then a Postulate all about the sins magic always knows?), and not in a way where the contradictions express something flavorful and complex.<br /> <br /> I like the effects of the Rogue's first two or three Conditions alright, though you may have gathered my feeling on making them actually Conditions rather than just &quot;if you are a Rogue, apply this Paradox modifier and get Mana from this situation.&quot; The Mana gain does seem a bit too high. Remember that under normal conditions, an exceptional success will return a <i>minimum</i> of five Mana if it's just equal to successes. The third or fourth Condition seems to me getting into overly defined territory. This is a &quot;kith,&quot; a more defined subset of Path &quot;style&quot; meant to layer on top of Path and Order. Don't make it too complicated and detailed, your character already has a lot of other stuff going on. Cut down to one or two simple but impactful changes to the character's approach to magic and to life.<br /> <br /> The Rogue's Act of Hubris seems like a recipe for arguments over what does and does not count as something that &quot;should happen.&quot; If you can't turn a poor person into a rich person because if a person is poor then they're definitionally supposed to be poor (shades of The Secret and prosperity gospel)... what <i>can</i> you do? Taken to its extreme conclusion, this logic suggests that everything is already as it should be and you just can't use magic. That <i>is</i> extreme, but... where's the line?<br /> <br /> Apologies if the feedback is presented as too harsh, I'm very low on sleep right now and spilling words dimly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 10-06-2023, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T11:32:29-07:00","id":1523727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1523695-classes-of-magic-subsystem?p=1523696#post1523696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting project! Though I would've framed Rogues with Mastigos-ness rather than Acanthus-ness.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a result of me breaking the Rogue archetype into a &quot;rogue/gambler&quot; and an &quot;assassin&quot;. There will be a Assassin Call which would probably fit what you had in mind. Here I followed mostly the idea of &quot;covert magic&quot; as a concept of &quot;stealth&quot; and added a lot of the gambler/lucky features that are often connected to rogues, hence the result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also feel the mini-template as is relies a bit too much on Conditions, though I can't think of succinct replacements... Perhaps giving a few free Praxes, and one or two mandatory Inurements, could replace some of the Gnostic Conditions? </div> </div> </div>The main reason that I used Conditions (probably also answers <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a>) is that I wanted those features to be &quot;behaviour shaping&quot; traits, which both cause the character to behave in a certain way and that gain &quot;enlightenment&quot; by following their Archetype (which is very Mage-y imo) in the form of Arcane Beats. Conditions serve both of those purposes, so representing those capabilities through a Condition system felt natural for me (similar to how certain Hunter features are tied to low Integrity with Conditions). So Conditions just worked, pretty much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T15:32:23-07:00","id":1523741,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, like Agenda Conditions from Demon and Satiety Conditions from Beast. Gotcha.<br /> <br /> Mmm, maybe we can still cut down some by making only one Gnostic Condition persistent, and making others situational/temporary?<br /> <br /> Or maybe we just want more examples \u2014 interested in how Fighters and Wizards/Sorcerers fit here, for opposite reasons <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T17:16:36-07:00","id":1523745,"title":"","content":"First, just to make sure- your criticism is very much welcomed and the feedback doesn't feel too harsh. Constructive criticism is always a good thing, and this is why I publish those things.<br /> <br /> As for the comments themselves-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1523695-classes-of-magic-subsystem?p=1523710#post1523710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what use the Postulates are, as they seesaw between simply restating the Awakening setting premise and replacing parts of it with an overbroad shrug. They seem self-contradictory (if all lies are equal, how are there living facts within magic defining the lost Time Before? if no teaching is a sin for magic knows not sin, why is there then a Postulate all about the sins magic always knows?), and not in a way where the contradictions express something flavorful and complex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, the Postulates are not some system or in-game terms or something like that. They were made as my own &quot;design guidelines&quot;- things to keep in mind when I write those Calls down. The reason is that at as things stand, I was not sure how diverged the interpretations of the Calls about magic are going to be, so I needed to keep something in mind. It should be noted that I have initially considered Calls as replacements for Orders (you might see some remnants of it in the writeup), so while I did the mental link between the Postulates and the outcome it might be less clear for others. Basically, they should represent something that all Calls agree upon, and that there is no Call that violates it. It needs to be seen how relevant they eventually will be, which depends on how far am I going to diverge from the :&quot;canon&quot; perception.<br /> <br /> Just to make sure we are all on the same page, here is what the Postulates are meant to express:<br /> <br /> - Magic exists (pretty basic)<br /> - All <i>Calls </i>are equal in their perception of magic (&quot;lies&quot; mean &quot;Calls&quot; in this regards. It means that no Call is the true &quot;master of magic&quot; or is somehow &quot;closer&quot; to understand magic than the others- so no &quot;Wizards are the true masters of magic&quot; kind of thing)<br /> - There was a World Before which have been retroactively removed from the world (Exarch shenanigans) <br /> - fuck around and you'll get Paradox (so no Call can have a feature to ignore Paradox).<br /> <br /> So yeah, I don't think that are too weird, and potentially are not needed, but again it is just to make sure I &quot;stay in lines&quot; when writing those down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like the effects of the Rogue's first two or three Conditions alright, though you may have gathered my feeling on making them actually Conditions rather than just &quot;if you are a Rogue, apply this Paradox modifier and get Mana from this situation.&quot; The Mana gain does seem a bit too high. Remember that under normal conditions, an exceptional success will return a <i>minimum</i> of five Mana if it's just equal to successes. The third or fourth Condition seems to me getting into overly defined territory. This is a &quot;kith,&quot; a more defined subset of Path &quot;style&quot; meant to layer on top of Path and Order. Don't make it too complicated and detailed, your character already has a lot of other stuff going on. Cut down to one or two simple but impactful changes to the character's approach to magic and to life. </div> </div> </div>Like, the main question I have here is &quot;are there too many features, or is it just their mechanization as Conditions&quot;? Because If it is the later, I personally don't have an issue with it but I also don't have a strong attachment for not calling them &quot;Conditions&quot;. I explained my rational for why they were made so, but I can, like, replace the Act of Hubris with Chained by Events (I wasn't sure about it anyway), make Bountiful Luck into a non-Condition mechanic (just give it some fancy name), and so just reman with 2 Gnostic Conditions. This both reduce the amount of moving parts and reduce the number of Conditions to 2, which I still want them to be as such as it does serves my goal as explained.<br /> <br /> We could, however, make one Condition into Persistent (gained at Gnosis 3) and change the other into Temporary one, but it would require some thought about how to redesign them (probably Out of Pattern is the Persistent one and Sly Hands is the temporary one, but I need to consider how to gain it).<br /> <br /> Again, thanks for the feedback, and feel free to give more comments both about those subjects or in the future <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T10:27:55-07:00","id":1523825,"title":"","content":"<i>Bountiful Luck</i> is pretty interesting. Ironically, it does not gain much benefit from Conditions like Inspired, which is something Fate magic could grant. It can be powerful with the right setup, but the once per chapter limit prevents it from being abused.<br /> <br /> Regarding <i>Out of Pattern</i>, I am concerned that in extreme situations, where the mage needs to throw everything at a problem, it might be too detrimental. When facing a dangerous spirit, escaping a peril in the Underworld or dealing with guardians of a piece of Infrastructure, natural law is not a primary concern when everything would be abnormal to a Sleeper. Since the objective is to incentivize certain behaviour patterns, I think including an exception for non-mundane situations would be helpful.<br /> <br /> <i>Sly Hands</i> is pretty cool mechanically, but the name seems to suggest a smooth criminal, a precise conman. The mechanics, however, are about the moment a twist of fate happens, landing a Rogue in some hot water. I think the name should reflect that. Curiously, if this is used often by players, it effectively becomes the inverse of Reliable Talent.<br /> <br /> <i>Chained by Events</i> feels like it errs a bit on the side of punishment. You either operate under a Ban and take significant setbacks, or your Gnosis takes a penalty. I feel like the Arcane Beat is not a counterbalance to losing dice on your power stat, since it affects Clashes of Wills, spell control, mana per turn limit and spellcasting ability.<br /> <br /> The Call itself feels strongly Acanthus by design, which makes the new Act of Hubris feel off. Acanthus are all about taking charge of their own fate, embracing Choice &amp; Consequence, rather than keeping their head down and be pulled along by the currents of fate. Similarly, Rogues navigate outside the law, using superlative skill and wit to sneak in a win. So I imagine its supernatural archtype would have an emphasis on defying fate, on finding ways to trick prophecy.<br /> <br /> Hopefully that proved helpful, I think this is a pretty cool concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-08-2023, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T17:15:07-07:00","id":1523842,"title":"","content":"How do the Calls fit into Mage society? What are the ideas for other Callings? Are these inherent to the template, or is there a way to get them after Awakening? How do they fit into the cosmology?<br /> <br /> Personally, the first &quot;Class&quot; that comes to mind for an adapted Call is that of a D&amp;D Warlock; ie Pact Magic. Maybe you didn't get to the Watchtower on your own but instead made a deal with a Supernal Being during the Awakening, probably in place of the normal Intercession. No impact on actually if someone gets the chance to Awaken, only would assist those who struggle with Intercession. So let's see what I can come up with off the top of my head.<br /> Act of Hubris would involve keeping to the deal, increased Paradox would map to challenging the role of Supernal Being, Magical Symbolism would take the form of Invocation/Intercession between the mundane and the magical, tying the role of the middle man/advocate to their magic. Rote Skills would be Politics and Socialize, maybe with Drive or Ride for a physical skill if one is required, representing the journey/separation between the Fallen and the Supernal.<br /> <br /> It's not the worst concept, but I'm not happy with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T02:37:23-07:00","id":1523867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1523695-classes-of-magic-subsystem?p=1523842#post1523842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the Calls fit into Mage society? What are the ideas for other Callings? Are these inherent to the template, or is there a way to get them after Awakening? How do they fit into the cosmology?</div> </div> </div> </div>In turns of fitting the cosmology of Mt:Aw- I think about it as &quot;symbols&quot;: each Call represents a different wat where magic is viewed and practiced. You can think about each Call as a Symbolic Archetype (the Quintessential Trickster, Scholar, Fighter and so forth), and by acting along that role, the Awakened discover a different way to use their magic and new ways to gain Enlightenment- yet at the cost of self limitation. So in a way, it is some sort of Paradigm from Ascension, only a bit backwards? You create self limitations in casting magic by binding yourself to a symbolic view and use and magic, which in turn grants greater understanding of the world (through the use of tools, skills, mana and Arcane Experience).<br /> <br /> As for the Warlock- looks cool, even though I am not going to go 1 to 1 with D&amp;D for the interpertations of the Classes (Warlock, for example, is planned to be broken to Warlock/Witch/Summoner/Sorcerer, Sorcerer will be broken to Dynast/Wilder/Maybe something else, Ranger and Druid will be unified, and so forth).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T02:50:03-07:00","id":1523868,"title":"","content":"First happy to hear you like the concept! as for specific concerns-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1523695-classes-of-magic-subsystem?p=1523825#post1523825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding <i>Out of Pattern</i>, I am concerned that in extreme situations, where the mage needs to throw everything at a problem, it might be too detrimental. When facing a dangerous spirit, escaping a peril in the Underworld or dealing with guardians of a piece of Infrastructure, natural law is not a primary concern when everything would be abnormal to a Sleeper. Since the objective is to incentivize certain behaviour patterns, I think including an exception for non-mundane situations would be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the idea is less about how Sleepers view it and more about how the character views it, so I am a bit warry to say &quot;not influential when monsters are involved&quot;. However, perhaps I should have been clear at this bit that the Call Tools specifically don't invalidate this Condition- that is, superstitions (as long as they are well understood/described) are a valid way to &quot;get around&quot; it- like throw a bit of salt on a Guardian of the Underworld and you can cast a power Death spell which would rend it apart, or make a spirit go under a ladder in order to use Forces to strike it with lightning as a form of &quot;bad luck&quot;. You can think of it as a method for rogues to &quot;lay traps&quot;. And if the players don't want to play along those rules, well, that's ok? They gain the penalty of +2 for the Paradox role on their spell, and do not gain an Arcane Beat where they might have gotten one. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Chained by Events</i> feels like it errs a bit on the side of punishment. You either operate under a Ban and take significant setbacks, or your Gnosis takes a penalty. I feel like the Arcane Beat is not a counterbalance to losing dice on your power stat, since it affects Clashes of Wills, spell control, mana per turn limit and spellcasting ability.<br /> <br /> The Call itself feels strongly Acanthus by design, which makes the new Act of Hubris feel off. Acanthus are all about taking charge of their own fate, embracing Choice &amp; Consequence, rather than keeping their head down and be pulled along by the currents of fate. Similarly, Rogues navigate outside the law, using superlative skill and wit to sneak in a win. So I imagine its supernatural archtype would have an emphasis on defying fate, on finding ways to trick prophecy. </div> </div> </div>As I mentioned, I considered to move Chained by Events into an Act of Hubris, and I currently consider cutting the additional Act of hubris all together (I think that there is enough material for a Call even without it), so I may just cut it altogether.<br /> <br /> Also, just to clarify (which I think it also answers <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a>), while Rogues do rely on luck, they are not meant to be directly tied to the Acanthus (that is, any Path could adopt any Call- there might be more Acanthus who adopt this Call, but nothing mechanical is meant to limit it in such a way). Also, I am still going back and forth about the ability to adopt a Call post-Awakening, and sometimes even consider rules for changing a Call later in game. Still rough thoughts, nothing set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T06:23:09-07:00","id":1523873,"title":"","content":"So before I'm moving for other Calls, I want to first decide on the format that will be used for each Call (like, what is gained from it). So currently this is the next draft- again, any constructive criticism will be welcomed: <br /> <br /> Each Call gives the following-<br /> <br /> 1) Libation- a name for the Mana gaining method, similar to Oblation but gives an amount of Mana equal to Gnosis rating<br /> 2) Gnostic Conditions- two Persistent and one Temporary (gained by activating the Libation)<br /> 3) Act of Hubris (Medium rating)<br /> 4) Magical Symbolism (Tools and Skills)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Libation: Bountiful Luck</b></span><br /> <br /> Rogues dance on the strings of fate, allowing them to find enlightenment at pure chance. Once per chapter, when making a role related to their Call Rote Skills and achieving an Exceptional Success, they can choose to \u201cliquify\u201d their luck into Mana, gaining an amount of Mana equal to their Gnosis rating in the roll instead of the regular effect of an Exceptional Success. The role will still be treated as a Success in whatever it was meant to achieve.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Gnostic Conditions</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Out of Pattern (</b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Persistent</b></span><b>)</b><br /> <br /> Rogues view magic as happy coincidences bestowed upon them through randomness and chance, and trying to enforce that act through force disrupts their delicate symbolism. When casting magic in a way which visually violates the natural laws and does not apply the Call tools (such as superstitions and lucky charms), add 2 dice to their Paradox roll.<br /> <b>Source</b>: adopting the Rogue Call<br /> <b>Arcane Beat</b>: the character avoids solving a problem using magic at a significant cost in order to avoid using it vulgarly.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Unbalanced Scales</b></span><br /> <br /> Rogues put their lives in the hands of chance, betting on lives on a daily basis- yet even if they win, Luck demands compensation. While under this Condition, the Rogue suffers from -1 for rolls involving the Call Skill in which they have a Specialty. In case this does not apply, choose the Call Skill with highest rating, and in case of tie choose randomly to which is applies.<br /> <b>Source</b>: activating Bountiful Luck<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> rake a Dramatic Failure instead of a regular Failure in a roll involving the affected Skill. Doing so grants an Arcane Beat instead of a regular Beat.<br /> <b>Arcane Beat</b>: as described above.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Act of Hubris: Chained by Events</b></span><br /> <br /> <i><b>Wisdom 4-7, Medium / Understanding</b></i><br /> <br /> Rogues are so used to relying on their luck that they become imprints of it- they must follow a set of rules, or otherwise they\u2019ll fall from the Pattern and become forsaken by the luck that carries them. Choose a certain obligation, equivalent for the Ban of a Rank 1 ephemeral entity. Violating this Ban is considered an Act of Hubris. It can not be considered as a Call Tool even if it covers the same territory as a superstition or a similar concept.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Magic Symbolism: Taking a Chance</b></span><br /> <br /> Rogues always lurk between the cracks in reality, being favoured by fortune as they put themselves in peril. As such, rogues are always driven to situations where it is all or nothing, gambling on their lives to either win it all or fall to the Abyss. However, that doesn\u2019t mean that they are fools- they always make sure that luck is in their favour, drawing it through their personal rituals and charms, as well as maintaining that they are skillful enough at getting out of trouble as they are in getting into them, just to make sure they have a way out if and when luck will fail them.<br /> <br /> Call Tools: Superstitions, lucky charms, dice and games<br /> <br /> Call Rote Skills: Enigmas, Larceny, Socialise<br /> <br /> ************************************************** ***********<br /> <br /> So what do you think about the second draft? My most significant question is about the disadvantage of Unbalanced Scales, as I don't want it to be too severe to the point that players won't use the Libation in the first place. \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T07:04:42-07:00","id":1523877,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m admittedly bad at crunching numbers, but compared to Sin-Eaters using their Keys (the closest equivalent, I think), I believe they get less oomph for more ouch, so it feels okay?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T05:50:22-07:00","id":1523913,"title":"","content":"Next Call is now up- again, feel free to share criticism:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Fighter</b></span><br /> <br /> <i><b>Magic Forge the Soul</b></i><br /> <br /> In the eyes of the fighter, magic is only as strong as the vessel which channels it. A healthy mind in a healthy body leads to a healthy soul- that\u2019s the essence. While the Awakened can move mountains and command the gods, magic always takes its toll- and if the soul is weak, the furnace of magic will consume it, shattering it into pieces. If the soul is strong, it will be forged to its ideal form, actualising the Awakened Will without falling into the pitfalls of hubris.<br /> <br /> As such, fighters always care about their physical form and mental state- while some fighters might take it to the extreme, most seek the perfected form which would lead to perfected will and perfected magic. While some of the Awakened use spells in order to augment their bodies, for the fighters this is commonly being viewed as \u201ccheating\u201d- you merely adjust the body, you do not truly forge it, and as such you become dependent on magic which would bring to your downfall. A true Awakened does not need magic in order to solve their problems- it merely comes as an expression of their own enlightenment, reached through hard work and effort. Only after the body and the mind are being properly trained to their human maximum, then magic could truly offer to transcend their physical limitations, crossing the edge between a human and a god- for only the strongest and flawless blades would not shatter in the inferno which is Ascension.<br /> <br /> In order to measure the purity of the soul, however, it must be tested. Fighters as such commonly do so by putting themselves into conflicts- going through both mundane and supernatural dangers, striving through mental and physical hardships as one. Participating in the Duel Arcana, fighting against lesser gods, testing their skills in competitions and working all night without any sleep- all of those forge the soul of the fighter, allowing it to draw upon greater magic. As they view their body as the vessel of magic, they often imbue themselves with supernatural capabilities, either weaving the magic into their own Patterns or combine it with their movements and strikes. Yet they must always make sure to never become dependent on it- for this is how the Abyss pollutes the body, mind and soul, turning the paragon of excellence into a crippled husk.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Libation: Blood of the Enemy</b></span><br /> <br /> Fighters draw their worth from their antithesis, finding enlightenment in proper adversary. Once per chapter, when fighting a \u201cfair fight\u201d against an enemy and causing the target at least one point of lethal damage, the fighter can exchange that one point of damage in order to gain an amount of Mana equal to their Gnosis. Generally, a \u201cfair fight\u201d means not using traps, ambushes, poisons and other forms of deceit, as well as using weapons of \u201cproper level\u201d against the threat- such as mundane weapons against mortals and magic against spirits.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Gnostic Conditions</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Living Vessel (Persistent)</b></span><br /> <br /> Fighters do not view themselves as users of magic, but as capacitors who contain it within them. For them, magic must be channelled through their own bodies as a vessel- or otherwise, the Abyss will lash out as they corrupt their own souls with hubris. When casting a spell that does not act through the fighter\u2019s body or tools directly (such as throwing a lightning bolt instead of channelling it through a fist or sword), add 2 dice to the Paradox roll.<br /> <br /> Source: adopting the Fighter Call<br /> <br /> Arcane Beat: every time you put yourself in a significant hindrance or risk due to the casting limitation, gain an Arcane Beast<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Soul Blade</b></span><br /> <br /> Fighters bond with their dedicated weapons, weaving them into their own Patterns. While under this Condition, the character gains a +1 for all rolls using the weapon that triggered the Condition and -2 when using other weapons or ritual tools until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> Source: activating Blood of the Enemy<br /> <br /> Resolution: either defeating or being defeated by the chosen enemy.<br /> <br /> Arcane Beat: defeat the enemy, either by killing them or receive a surrender.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Act of Hubris: Rusting the Blade</b></span><br /> <br /> <i><b>Wisdom 4-7, Medium / Understanding</b></i><br /> <br /> Fighters believe that magic is not a tool- it is a blessing bestowed on those who are perfected, and avoiding to test the blade leads to its rust, and as such to hubris. Refusing a fair challenge when proposed to them by another, be it a duel, a game or a competition, is considered as an Act of Hubris for fighters.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Magic Symbolism: Tools of War</b></span><br /> <br /> Fighters are made for battle- their bodies are forged, their minds are sharpened, their souls bear the scars of their conflict. Each fighter is a living weapon meant to bring ruin upon their enemies while protecting whatever they hold dear. As such, the fighters express their existence as a vessel of war through the tools of war themselves, channelling their magic with their bound weapons, proof of their victories and their very bodies, which are deadly weapons by themselves.<br /> <br /> Call Tools: Weapons and armour, martial arts, trophies won in battle<br /> <br /> Call Route Skills: Athletics, Warfare, Weaponry<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Philosophy of Magic</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>On the Paths</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Acanthus</b>: always follow your oaths and the agreements you made with both allies and enemies, for those who break them draw the ire of the gods.<br /> <br /> <b>Mastigos</b>: first break the mind of the enemy, then break their body. Those who can\u2019t withstand the first test are not worthy of the second.<br /> <br /> <b>Moros</b>: always pay respect to the dead, even if they were your enemies, for all are equal in death. Otherwise, the dead will demand their due.<br /> <br /> <b>Obrimos</b>: a proper vessel of the divine can hold the power of the gods in their hands- yet to be consumed with destruction will destroy you as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Thyrsus</b>: to truly forge one\u2019s body and mind, they must leave the comfort of civilization behind. Learn the ways of tooth and claw before you dare to lift a sword.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>On the Orders</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Adamantine Arrow</b>: always fight with honour and respect your rival. This is what turns simple violence into a battle, and distinguishes men from beasts.<br /> <br /> <b>Guardians of the Veil</b>: the soul is purified through the cycles of reincarnation- and those who have flawed souls should return to the cycle so they may be forged anew.<br /> <br /> <b>Mysterium</b>: one must know their enemy if they are to defeat them. Understand their weakness, plan your strategy, and when they are the least prepared- attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Silver Ladder</b>: to be a true leader of the people, you must represent their values- be at your most excellence, and others will follow your footsteps.<br /> <br /> <b>Free Council</b>: humanity has forged countless tools of war and countless ways to destroy itself. Learn from their mistakes so you won\u2019t do the same.<br /> <br /> <b>Seers of the Throne</b>: the masses only respect power- unite them under a single will through force, and send them to die with your name on their lips.<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere</b>: weak souls only lay the mind to waste and the body to rot. Take them to forge your own, for the weak don\u2019t deserve your mercy.<br /> <br /> <b>Scelesti</b>: blade has no worth when it lays on the wall, accumulating dust. Bath yourself in blood and cut them all until you\u2019ll break- that\u2019s how you achieve true excellence.<br /> <br /> <b>Banishers</b>: magic is corruptive by nature, for it creates dependency and weakens the body, mind and soul. Those who rely on it are weak and corrupted, and should be rooted out.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>On the Arcana</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Death</b>: strike at through the cracks between the body and the soul, and your enemy will fall with one swipe.<br /> <br /> <b>Fate</b>: every blade has its destined battle, choose carefully.<br /> <br /> <b>Forces</b>: nature has its own arsenal, use them for your advantage.<br /> <br /> <b>Life</b>: the base for all is a healthy body. Guarantee that before you move forward.<br /> <br /> <b>Matter</b>: the perfect weapon is the one you make yourself.<br /> <br /> <b>Mind</b>: the strongest will is the one to win the battle- make sure yours won\u2019t break first.<br /> <br /> <b>Prime</b>: only those who are worthy can bear the weapons of the gods.<br /> <br /> <b>Space</b>: never let your enemy escape, crush their exit paths as you crush their soul.<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit</b>: a god can be killed if you have the right weapon.<br /> <br /> <b>Time</b>: learn from the past defeats, be prepared for future victories.<br /> <br /> <b>Abyss</b>: the rust which breaks the blade.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-14T17:34:39-07:00","id":1524076,"title":"","content":"So while I made some advancements on this projects, I always kept feeling like I'm hitting my head against a wall and that I somehow overcomplicate things. That feeling just made it very hard for me to make any advances in this project, as I kept feeling like there must be a simpler way to get what I want, and that there are too many moving parts in this splat. After giving it some thought, I eventually came to the conclusion that I really was overcomplicating this- I wanted Calls to be a behavioral system that shapes magic, and as such I really should have just made the Calls into what they needed to be- a Condition which grants Arcane Beats. As such, I've ditched most of the other features (those probably could be better adapted as Merits which require the Call Condition in order to be bought), as well keeping the Magic Symbolism and Call Tools (which seems to be a pretty standard part of Mage splats). However, instead of granting 3 Route Skills (which, again, overlap with Order), the character instead chooses a single free Specialty among the three Call Skills which are presented. This give some variety within the Calls and I think is a somewhat more elegant solution than the current system. As it is a much simpler solution, it also helped me to write up all of my &quot;Tier 1 Warrior Calls&quot; (where Tier 1 refers to &quot;standard D&amp;D classes&quot; concepts). I am yet to write a bit of fluff in regards to a &quot;Awakening to the Call&quot;, so currently it is mostly mechanics. Please let me know what you think!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Rogue: Magic is Serendipitous</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Rogue (Persistent)</b></span><br /> <br /> You are a rogue- master of trickery and mischief who is carried by luck. As a rogue, you view magic as a providence brought from fate, the gods, the universe or whatever name you give to the Powers that Be. As such, your spells must also flow with the course of luck, for disrupting it might summon the Abyss. When casting a spell, if your magic is actualized as something which could be explained as coincidence or happy occurrence (such as a lightning striking the enemy during rain or a small fortune being found on the floor), you gain 2 free Reach for the spell. However, if the spell is cast in a manner which is vulgar and obviously magical, you suffer from a +2 modifier for the Paradox roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcane Beat</b>: whenever you manage to use trickery against your enemy and succeed, you gain an Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Magic Symbolism: Luck</b></span><br /> <br /> Call Tools: lucky charms, games of chance<br /> <br /> Call Specialities: Enigmas, Larceny, Socialise<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Fighter: Magic Forge the Soul</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Fighter (Persistent)</b></span><br /> <br /> You are a fighter- master of warfare and weaponry. As a fighter, you see magic as being only as strong as the vessel which bears it- your body, and as such the excellence of the body is required in order to reach the greatest levels of magic, and that the body must serve as the spell\u2019s perfect vessel. When casting a spell which is channelled through your body, weapons or armour (as as enhancing the strength of a punch or cloaking a sword with flame), you gain 2 free Reach for the spell. However, when casting a spell without using the body as a vessel, you suffer from a +2 modifier for the Paradox roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcane Beat</b>: whenever you solve a problem without magic when it could have been done easily otherwise while putting yourself or your allies at risk, you gain an Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Magic Symbolism: Tools of War</b></span><br /> <br /> Call Tools: trophies of the enemy, weapons and armour<br /> <br /> Call Specialities: Athletics, Warfare, Weaponry<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Monk: Magic is Everywhere</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Monk (Persistent)</b></span><br /> <br /> You are a monk- mystical warrior trained in emulating the Supernal through your body and soul. As a monk, you view magic as a result of spiritual enlightenment and freedom from physical constraints, which can only be achieved through meditation, discipline and rigid training, meant to embody aspects of the everyday world within their body and soul. Choose a certain aspect of the world- this could be an animal, weather, trade, location, element and so forth. This aspect serves as your Martial Art Style. While casting spells that resonate with your Style, you gain 2 free Reach. When casting a spell which violates that style, however, you suffer from a +2 to the Paradox roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcane Beat</b>: whenever your character sacrifices their attachment to the world at a significant cost, you gain an Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Magic Symbolism: World Apart</b></span><br /> <br /> Call Tools: meditation accessories, objects resonating with their Style<br /> <br /> Call Specialities: Athletics, Brawl, Empathy<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Ranger: The World is Magical</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Ranger (Persistent)</b></span><br /> <br /> You are a ranger- a master of the hunt and stalker of the wilderness. As a ranger, you view magic as part of the environment- the world itself is filled with magic, and has a will of its own which must not be defied. As such, your magic must fit the world around you, or otherwise your magic will pollute the world with the foul touch of the Abyss. Whenever you cast a spell which fits or utilises the local environment (such as the use of local flora and fauna, the current state of lighting or weather or objects which are locally present), you gain 2 free Reach. However, if your spells outright defies the local environment or tries to violently change its properties, you suffer from a +2 modifier to the Paradox roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcane Beat</b>: whenever you manage you bring down a foe by exploiting their weakness or your understanding of the environment, you gain an Arcane Beat<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Magic Symbolism: the Great Hunt</b></span><br /> <br /> Call Tools: traps, vehicles or tools which ease movement<br /> <br /> Call Specialities: Drive, Ride, Stealth<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Barbarian: Magic Unbound</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Barbarian (Persistent)</b></span><br /> <br /> You are a barbarian- a force of destruction embodied in human form. As a barbarian, you believe that the mind, or the ego, is the barrier which blocks the natural use of magic, and that by killing your own sense of self and delving into your instincts and raw impulses you can become one with the world and actualise true magic. As such, magic must be an untamed force that is born out of raw passion, while trying to bind it through words and logic you sin against its natural state, allowing the Abyss to enter the world. Whenever you cast a spell that aligns with either your Vice or Virtue, you gain 2 free Reach. However, if the use of the spell outright violates those Anchors, you suffer from a +2 to the Paradox roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcane Beat</b>: every time you follow your passion instead of a rational course of action at the cost of putting yourself or your goals at risk, gain an Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Magic Symbolism: Untamed Rage</b></span><br /> <br /> Call Tools: drugs and intoxicants, tattoos<br /> <br /> Call Specialities: Animal Ken, Brawl, Weaponry<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Paladin: Chivalry is Magical</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Paladin (Persistent)</b></span><br /> <br /> You are a paladin- a follower of a personal code of conduct which defines \u201cright\u201d from \u201cwrong\u201d. As a paladin, you have a strong faith in your ideals and values, leading your actions to follow them and bring honourable life- and as you believe, magic is bestowed upon you as a blessing from serving as a paragon of those values. As such, all acts of magic which serve those ideals are honourable, while those who violate them are punished by the wrath of the Abyss. Choose a certain code of conduct, made out of three clauses derived from your Virtue. Whenever your spell is meant to advance those values or behaviour in the world, gain 2 Reach for free. However, if your spell\u2019s use breaks that code or disrupts those values or their progression in the world, you suffer from a +2 modifier to the Paradox roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcane Beat</b>: whenever you make a significant sacrifice in the name of your ideals, you gain an Arcane Beat<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Magic Symbolism: Beloved by Heaven</b></span><br /> <br /> Call Tools: blessed weaponry, speeches and warsongs<br /> <br /> Call Specialities: Empathy, Socialise, Weaponry<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Slayer: Magic is Corrupted</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Slayer (Presistent)</b></span><br /> <br /> You are a slayer- a self mutilated blood mage that burns their own lives and the lives of others as they practise foul magic. As a slayer, you believe that magic is the force which grants life to matter, a vital force which animates the flesh and burns in their blood, called Ki, nephesh, Ka and so forth. As such, magic is actualised through blood and sacrifice, and is in essence an accursed tool which feeds upon life force. Whenever you cast a spell which is meant to corrupt, destroy, curse or defile in some manner the world around you, yourself or your enemies, you gain 2 free Reach. However, if your spell is meant to be used in a constructive manner, such as healing, fixing or helping society overall, you suffer from a +2 to the Paradox roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcane Beat</b>: whenever you cause the desecration of an object or value which you hold dear, you gain an Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Magic Symbolism: Blood and Sacrifice</b></span><br /> <br /> Call Tools: fresh blood, ritual blades<br /> <br /> Call Specialities: Athletics, Investigation, Medicine<br /> \u200b<br /> (Note: the Slayer refers to the Blood Hunter Class from Critical Role, included here due to my OCD).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T14:35:16-07:00","id":1524118,"title":"","content":"So I completed all of my &quot;Tier 1&quot; Calls. You can find them in the following Google Docs documents.<br /> <br /> I have divided it according to the &quot;four roles&quot; of D&amp;D classes:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mPlADBK76RjOItetG-cYjdEQ7IAJi6IsOu-XV-0TWzw/edit#heading=h.xvbui2jnza95\" target=\"_blank\">Warriors</a>- Barbarian, Fighter, Monk (potentially will be moved to Priest), Paladin, Ranger, Slayer (potentially will be moved to Sage)<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vsWtzZPIbydYqaI9lqITfeQTqgoqBS-Tzo0pnN6vb00/edit#heading=h.2cdo6p90l4gl\" target=\"_blank\">Expert</a>- Artificer, Rogue, Bard<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KwS3BdQZhHNUGZC_5dDi8-OsHP4OYbTGegXRh52YBnA/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Sage</a>- Dynast (potentially will be moved to Expert), Psion, Wizard<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bRUw-hclSU6cAMPkDAZ_EOzT1RljnsPgnmmKMa-zsTc/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Priest</a>- Cleric, Druid, Mystic, Warlock (potentially will be moved to Sage)<br /> <br /> As mentioned, Slayer is a rebrand of the Blood Hunter from Critical Role, while Dynast refers to Sorcerer (potentially will be renamed back to Sorcerer, depending if I'll develop the Sha'ir to its own Call) and the Mystic refers to Dragonlance's Age of Mortal Class (of which I am a big fan). Again, let me know if you have any comments about this piece while I am working on Tier 2 of the Calls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 10-17-2023, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-17T10:46:13-07:00","id":1524200,"title":"","content":"So I decided to break the Doc into 4 different ones simply due to the large amount of pages we have already in this stage, which made it annoying for me to roll through. I've also added a new Warrior Call which takes a different approach for magic using, being a bit more &quot;exotic&quot;. I'm adding it here for review, so let me know if you prefer more things like this or what we had up to this point.<br /> <br /> <b>Incarnate: Magic Demands Form</b><br /> <br /> <b>Incarnate (Persistent)</b><br /> <br /> You are an Incarnate- a shaper of arcane energies which manifests armoury out of the ether. As an incarnate, you view magic as a raw potential of creation, shaped through imagination and willpower to create whatever the Awakened Will demand, for all magic is merely aspects of the soul manifested. Choose a physical form for each of the Arcana, taking the forms of weapons, armours, jewellery and so on. The vessel serves as a symbolic and mythical tool of magic that evolves with the Arcana rating of the incarnate, which can be summoned using 1 Willpower and dismissed for free. The incarnate may have only a number of such vessels manifested in the same time equal to their Gnosis rating divided by 2, rounded down, minimum of 1. When casting a spell while the proper vessel is manifested, the Awakened gains 2 free Reach (in a case numerous Arcana are required, all such vessels are needed). If none of the required vessels are being manifested, however, you gain a +2 to the Paradox roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcane Beat</b>: whenever you create a lasting artwork representing a major event or emotion, you gain an Arcane Beat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T14:43:58-07:00","id":1524288,"title":"","content":"So I completed my Tier 2 Calls. Just one more bunch and I will finish the easy part of Condition writeups before fleshing them more out (and potentially adding Call Merits). I've also made a few revisions to currently written Calls. The current list is as follows:<br /> <br /> Warrior Calls- Barbarian, Fighter, Incarnate, Monk, Paladin, Ranger, Slayer, Templar\u200b<br /> <br /> Expert Calls- Artificer, Assassin, Bard, Beguiler, Dynast, Grafter, Hacker, Rogue, Wilder\u200b<br /> <br /> Sage Calls- Alchemist, Defiler, Psion, Runecaster, Sorcerer, Summoner, Witch, Wizard\u200b<br /> <br /> Priest Calls- Cleric, Druid, Exorcist, Geomancer, Mystic, Necromancer, Oracle, Shaman, Warlock<br /> <br /> No more than 13 Calls to go (probably a bit less). \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T04:15:26-07:00","id":1524418,"title":"","content":"So it's been a while, but I've finally completed the base of this project, with 48 Call writeups. I'll probably take a short break while I'll consider what to do next (either add some fluff like I did with the Barbarian Call or potentially start writing Call Merits or something, also will try to think about potentially giving a certain mechanical benefit to each &quot;genre&quot; of Calls, like Warriors having something in common)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}